 <iati-activity default-currency="USD" hierarchy="1" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities">
  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-MNG155</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decent work is promoted through skills development, labour market programmes and services to facilitate transitions in the labour market with particular attention to women and youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mongolia continues to face a shortage of skilled workers, with youth unemployment at 14.7 per cent&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201d;more than twice the national rate of 5.9 per cent&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201d;and a NEET rate of 10 per cent. Labour force participation is declining, particularly among women, and the gender pay gap remains 17.4 per cent, according to the National Statistics Office.
        The Ministry of Family, Labour and Social Protection has declared 2026 the Year of Employment Promotion and introduced new Employment Promotion Programmes to strengthen skills, support green and digital transitions, and improve productivity. These measures aim to build labour&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2018;market&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2018;relevant skills, improve employability, and facilitate young people&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s transition into productive and sustainable jobs.
In line with these priorities, the ILO will continue supporting government, employers, and workers to advance youth employment. The Office will implement workplace innovations, organize youth job fairs and workplace visits, and promote smoother school&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2018;to&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2018;work transitions. In selected enterprises, the ILO will introduce SCORE&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2018;based workplace improvement training and document youth&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2018;centred workplace practices for wider learning. Lifelong learning and vocational training centres will also be engaged to strengthen young people&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s employability.
        Expected changes: 1&#xef;&#xbc;&#x2030; Youth employment is strengthened through comprehensive skills development and lifelong learning.
2&#xef;&#xbc;&#x2030; Informal workers and enterprises move toward formalization through integrated digital platforms&#xef;&#xbc;&#x203a; 3&#xef;&#xbc;&#x2030; ILO constituents&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; capacity is strengthened to implement effective green economy policies aligned with Just Transition guidance</narrative>
  </description>
